'' =====================================================================
'' conflict-testJ-polar-theta0.spin2  --  settles PLOT POLAR orientation
''   (where theta=0 points, and which way increasing theta rotates)
''
'' QUESTION: ch05 POLAR section carries an UNANCHORED claim about where the
''   zero angle sits and the rotation sense (flip risk).  POLAR maps the two
''   cursor coords to (rho, theta).  We need ground truth for:
''     (a) theta = 0   -> which screen direction? (East/right?  North/up?)
''     (b) increasing theta -> counter-clockwise (math) or clockwise (screen)?
''   (`POLAR 360` sets a full turn = 360 units, so theta is in degrees; the
''    default twopi sense is under test here -- yaml notes twopi -1/0 flip it.)
''
'' TWO-RAIL / SELF-BRACKET: draw four spokes from the center origin at
''   theta = 0, 90, 180, 270, each a distinct color, all rho=180:
''     RED=0  GREEN=90  BLUE=180  YELLOW=270.
''   The rig is self-checking: RED and BLUE MUST be COLLINEAR-OPPOSITE (0 vs
''   180) and GREEN/YELLOW MUST be the OPPOSITE pair, orthogonal to RED/BLUE.
''   If the four are not two orthogonal opposed pairs -> INCONCLUSIVE (we
''   know it), never a false positive.  A short RED stub at rho=90 double-marks
''   the 0 direction so it can't be confused with its 180 opposite.
''
''   Decide from RED: theta=0 points to the screen direction RED occupies;
''   then GREEN (90) tells the sense -- 90 deg CCW from RED = math (0=East,
''   CCW); 90 deg CW = screen convention.  Compare to whatever ch05 asserts.
''
'' READ (image-tools): find center (200,200); for each spoke color compute
''   its bearing from center (atan2 of a bright pixel) -> the 0-direction and
''   the 0->90 turn direction fall straight out.
'' =====================================================================

CON
  _clkfreq = 100_000_000

PUB main()
  debug(`PLOT PJ SIZE 400 400 BACKCOLOR BLACK)
  debug(`PJ ORIGIN 200 200 POLAR 360)                ' center origin; theta in degrees

  debug(`PJ RED    SET 0 0 LINE 180 0   3 255)        ' spoke theta=0    (RED)   <- the anchor
  debug(`PJ GREEN  SET 0 0 LINE 180 90  3 255)        ' spoke theta=90   (GREEN) <- sense probe
  debug(`PJ BLUE   SET 0 0 LINE 180 180 3 255)        ' spoke theta=180  (BLUE)  = opposite RED
  debug(`PJ YELLOW SET 0 0 LINE 180 270 3 255)        ' spoke theta=270  (YELLOW)= opposite GREEN
  debug(`PJ WHITE  SET 0 0 LINE 90  0   6 255)        ' short fat stub at theta=0 (double-mark 0)

  waitms(300)
  debug(`PJ save 'polarJ_wheel')
  waitms(500)
  repeat
